    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_text">• No account, no telemetry, no ads.\n• Passwords are never uploaded.\n• Location is only needed so Android returns Wi-Fi results; the app does not store it.\n• Work offline: scanner, signal analyzer, local device scan, saved networks.\n• Need internet: speed test, DNS and HTTPS diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="settings_troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="settings_troubleshooting_text">• Empty list: grant permissions and turn on the system location service.\n• Name or BSSID shows \"Unavailable\": permission missing or hidden by Android.\n• New scan does nothing: Android limits scans; wait a few minutes.\n• Speed test fails: check your internet connection or choose another server.\n• Few devices found: the router may use client isolation.</string>
